        55.37200927734375,
        248.6292724609375,
        63.95977020263672
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The primary distinction between VP-MBD and LP-MBD",
      "bbox": [
        63.9630012512207,
        70.4903564453125,
        298.8013916015625,
        79.39691925048828
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lies in their parameterization and the implications for tuning",
      "bbox": [
        54.0,
        82.44537353515625,
        298.80096435546875,
        91.35193634033203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and adaptation. In the VP-MBD formulation, the noise",
      "bbox": [
        54.0,
        94.400390625,
        298.80096435546875,
        103.30695343017578
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "schedule is governed by three parameters (β0, β1, T), where",
      "bbox": [
        54.0,
        106.19697570800781,
        298.7962341308594,
        115.95796203613281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the parameters are tightly coupled: modifying the diffusion",
      "bbox": [
